libnds: turn IME back on whenever a thread is resumed

libnds 426b9c98 dropped this line from the context switch, as the FIFO
thread no longer needed it. With libnds as it is now (223ccb43 included),
map loads hung on a 3DS in DSi mode, and the hang went with this line put
back. A check on every cothread yield caught the ARM7's FIFO thread
(fifoProcessThread) going to wait with IME 0 there; what leaves IME at 0 is
not found yet (melonDS never shows it). Until it is, a thread is resumed with
interrupts on, as before 426b9c98. Applied to the pinned libnds
(docker/Dockerfile, docker/versions.env); reported to BlocksDS.

diff --git a/source/common/cothread/context.s b/source/common/cothread/context.s
--- a/source/common/cothread/context.s
+++ b/source/common/cothread/context.s
@@ -45,6 +45,13 @@
     bic     r1, r1, #CPSR_FLAG_IRQ_DIS
     msr     spsr, r1
 
+    // Enable IME as well (as before 426b9c98): something leaves IME at 0
+    // when the ARM7's FIFO thread yields, not yet found; until it is, every
+    // thread resumes with interrupts on.
+    mov     r3, #0x4000000
+    mov     r4, #1
+    str     r4, [r3, #0x208]
+
     ldr     lr, [r0, #COTHREAD_INFO_CPU_PC_OFFSET]
 
     ldmia   r0, {r0-r12}
